# Operational scripts.
#
# Everything in scripts/ is TRACKED. This block used to be the other way round —
# a blanket `scripts/*` followed by 47 `!` negations — and the failure mode was
# always the same one: a script landed on disk, was wired into package.json, and
# was never added to the allow-list, so a fresh checkout got an npm script with
# no file behind it. It fails as "Cannot find module", long after the reason is
# visible. setupApi.js, setupUi.js, seedApi.js and startup.js each had to be
# rescued from it by hand; payWithDiscount.js — which `npm run setup` and
# `npm run setup:api` both call — was found missing from HEAD the same way.
#
# Ignoring by exception is the only shape that does not depend on someone
# remembering. Adding a script now needs no edit here.
#
# GENERATED files are the exception, by naming convention: anything written by a
# tool rather than by a person is called *.generated.json and is not committed,
# because it is reproduced in seconds from a live system and a stale copy would
# be believed rather than questioned.
#
#   scripts/perf/routes.generated.json         read off the live Express router
#                                              by scripts/perf/extract-routes.js
#   scripts/seed/registrations.generated.json  holds plaintext passwords and
#                                              describes one database's state;
#                                              regenerate it with
#                                              `npm --prefix Web run seed:ui`
#
# scripts/seed/panel-plan.json, meets.json and judges.json are NOT generated in
# this sense. They are DECISIONS about what the fixture is — hand-maintained and
# read by both stacks — so they stay tracked. A panel plan that existed only on
# the machine that drew it would let a second machine seat a 4-judge panel and
# score it as a 5, which produces a believable number rather than an error.
*.generated.json
